@startuml tpp-access-screen-flow
' Screen flow — review and withdraw one TPP's access. PROPOSAL, AI, 2026-09-19.
' Iteration 4 (SRC-ADR 7ed3eb1): the PSU authenticates on the IDP login screen, then manages one
' TPP's access on the consent screen in the browser. No cross-TPP overview. Stories: STORY-PSU-REVOKE.
title Review and withdraw a TPP's access — consent screen

state "SCR-TPP-REQUEST\n<i>TPP — entry point to manage access (how: Q-43)</i>" as Entry
state "SCR-IDP-LOGIN\n<i>CMP-PING — the IDP owns the login screen</i>" as Identify
state "SCR-CONSENT-MANAGE\n<i>CMP-CONSENT-SCREEN · RM-PSU-TPP-ACCESS</i>" as Manage
state "SCR-CONSENT-REVOKE-CONFIRM\n<i>CMP-CONSENT-SCREEN · RM-PSU-TPP-ACCESS</i>" as Confirm

[*] --> Entry
Entry --> Identify : open consent screen (Q-43)
Identify --> Manage : identified
Manage --> Confirm : "Withdraw access"
Confirm --> Manage : cancel
Confirm --> Manage : confirm — revokeTppAccess\n(consentStatus revokedByPsu; shown as withdrawn)
Manage --> [*] : back to the TPP

note right of Manage
  Shows only this TPP's access (the screen lives in its application).
  Last read by the TPP is open (Q-40).
end note
note right of Confirm
  States the consequence (UX-06). The TPP is not notified in MVP (Q-24):
  it learns at its next read, which RM-ACCESS-DECISION refuses.
  Is this "towards the ASPSP" (§14.15)? — Q-43.
end note
@enduml
